        "correct": false,
        "why": "It does not bring the system back."
      },
      {
        "text": "Reviving it with Apple Configurator",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right. From another Mac, over USB-C."
      },
      {
        "text": "Nothing; it must be replaced",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It can usually be revived."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ex-txsce94p",
    "version": 1,
    "section": "the-disk",
    "type": "quiz",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "drillable": true,
    "prompt": "How is an APFS container different from lesson 2's partitions?",
    "hint": "Who decides the sizes?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "text": "It can only hold one volume",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "It holds several."
      },
      {
        "text": "It is readable by Windows",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "APFS is not, without extra software."
      },
      {
        "text": "Each volume has a fixed size",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "That is the partition model."
      },
      {
        "text": "Its volumes share one pool of space",
        "correct": true,
        "why": "Right. None has a fixed size."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
